'' =====================================================================
'' conflict-testD-textstyle.spin2  --  informs F-205 (TEXTSTYLE)
''
'' QUESTION: what do PLOT TEXTSTYLE weight bits look like?  REF §7.0 says
''   default textStyle = 1; F-205 disputes what the weight bits MEAN
''   (manual: $00 = "light"; REF distillation implies %01 = normal).
''
'' TWO-RAIL DESIGN: draw the SAME string at styles $00,$01,$02,$03 down
''   the canvas.  The progression is the rail: if $00..$03 all render
''   IDENTICALLY the style byte is ignored (test inconclusive -> we know).
''   If they differ, we can read whether $00 is LIGHTER than $01 (default)
''   or heavier, and where the weight steps.  A big control string sample
''   ('WWWjjj000') maximizes stroke area to measure ink coverage.
''
'' READ (image-tools): per row, measure glyph ink coverage / stroke width;
''   confirm rows differ (rail), then order them by weight.
'' =====================================================================

CON
  _clkfreq = 100_000_000

PUB main()
  DEBUG(`PLOT P SIZE 320 240)

  DEBUG(`P SET 20 30)
  DEBUG(`P TEXT 30 $00 0 'WWWjjj000 s00')
  DEBUG(`P SET 20 85)
  DEBUG(`P TEXT 30 $01 0 'WWWjjj000 s01')
  DEBUG(`P SET 20 140)
  DEBUG(`P TEXT 30 $02 0 'WWWjjj000 s02')
  DEBUG(`P SET 20 195)
  DEBUG(`P TEXT 30 $03 0 'WWWjjj000 s03')

  waitms(300)
  DEBUG(`P SAVE 'textD_styles')
  waitms(500)
  repeat
